## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `npm test` | The app's tests (mocked API, no network) |
| `npm run typecheck` | TypeScript check of `src/` and `test/` |
| `npm run lint` | Biome lint and format check (`npx biome check --write .` fixes formatting) |
| `npm run check` | `check-app`: loads the app and checks its manifest, the annotations of every tool it registers, logos and README sections. Must exit 0. Before shipping run `npx create-agent-app check-app --strict`, which also fails on TODO text left in the manifest or README; a logo TODO in the Logos section that lists where you looked still passes. |
| `SERVICE_KEY=... npm run health` | The health check once against the real service (secrets from environment variables named like the manifest's `installationSecrets`; values are never printed) |
| `npx agentapps ...` | The Agent Apps CLI for the live test (install the app under an alias, set its secrets, call tools). It is the `@agentapps/cli` devDependency. **Never install the unscoped `agentapps` package from npm: it is an unrelated project.** |
| `npx create-agent-app --help` | Every scaffold and check option |

## Rules

- Every tool declares `readOnlyHint`, `destructiveHint`, `idempotentHint`, `openWorldHint` and
  `sensitive` explicitly; `sensitive` is true exactly for tools that are not read-only. Never
  infer them from the tool name.
- `agentapp.json` and the `createApp()` config in `src/app.ts` describe the same app; change
  both together (a test checks it).
- Logos come from the service's official brand resources only, with the source in the README.
  Never generate or draw one; leave a TODO instead.
- Installation secrets are set per installed alias: `agentapps config <alias> KEY:value`. Never print,
  log or commit a secret.
- Ask the user before any live call that writes, and before pushing or publishing.
- Code comments and docs in English.
